        "original_id": "7ebbaf3f-b01a-5150-b9bc-9006511b2149",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Films: Moonraker, The Spy Who Loved Me, Inspector Gadget, Le gendarme et les gendarmettes\n- People: Lewis Gilbert, Lois Chiles, Michael Lonsdale, Corinne Cléry, Richard Kiel, Catherine Serre, Nicaise Jean Louis\n- Roles: Jaws, Countess Labinsky\n- Topics: James Bond franchise\n\nFacts:\n- Lewis Gilbert directed Moonraker, and it was the third and final film in the series that he directed.\n- Moonraker co-stars Lois Chiles, Michael Lonsdale, Corinne Cléry, and Richard Kiel.\n- Richard Kiel was an American actor, voice artist, and comedian born on September 13, 1939.\n- Richard Kiel portrayed Jaws in the James Bond franchise films The Spy Who Loved Me in 1977 and Moonraker in 1979.\n- Catherine Serre played Countess Labinsky in Moonraker as one of Drax's \"perfect\" human specimens from his master race.\n- Catherine Serre also appeared in Le gendarme et les gendarmettes together with Nicaise Jean Louis, another Drax Girl from Moonraker.\n- Richard Kiel lampooned his Jaws role with a tongue-in-cheek cameo in Inspector Gadget in 1999.\n- Richard Kiel died on September 10, 2014.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
